---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { company, photo } from "../data/company";
import Testimonials from "../components/Testimonials.astro";
import CallStrip from "../components/CallStrip.astro";
const lead = photo("bromley-residential-street-tiled-roofs");
---

<Layout
  title="About Us | LeonEast Roofing & Building"
  description="LeonEast Roofing & Building is a roofing firm working out of Bromley. What we do, how we price, and what the 10 year workmanship guarantee actually covers."
  lead={lead}
>
  <section class="bg-carbon text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight">About us</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-mist">
          {company.name} is a roofing and building firm working out of Bromley, covering the
          towns around it. Roofs are what we do all day - repairs, re-roofs, flat roofs,
          chimneys and guttering - on the houses this part of south east London is actually
          made of.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src={lead} alt="A street of bay fronted terraced houses with tiled roofs and chimney stacks"
        class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover aspect-[4/3]" width="840" height="630"
        fetchpriority="high" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-carbon">How we price</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      We come and look first, every time. Nobody can diagnose a roof from a driveway, and a
      quote produced without going up is a guess with a number attached. There is no charge
      for the visit and nothing to sign afterwards.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      You get photographs of whatever we find before you get a figure. The quote is itemised,
      with the materials, the labour and the access on separate lines, and the total on it is
      the total on the invoice. If something genuinely hidden turns up once a roof is opened
      up - rot in the rafter feet, a chimney worse than it looked - it gets described, priced
      and agreed with you before anybody carries on.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-carbon">The guarantee</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      Every van in south London says "all work guaranteed" and it costs nothing to paint on.
      Ours is a dated, signed document specific to your job, handed over when we finish along
      with the photographs. {company.guaranteeYears} years on our workmanship: if water finds
      its way back through something we repaired, we come back and put it right at no cost.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      Materials carry their manufacturers' own cover on top, which varies from product to
      product, so your paperwork names the one that applies to your roof rather than quoting
      an average at you.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      A guarantee lasting a decade only works if the repairs do not come back, which is why
      failed material comes off rather than being sealed over, junctions get lead rather than
      a fillet of cement, and anything we cannot deal with on the day gets photographed and
      said out loud.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-carbon">Insurance and paperwork</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      We carry public liability insurance and are happy to show you the certificate - it
      takes ten seconds and almost nobody asks. {company.name} is a limited company
      registered in England and Wales. Where a job is going through a buildings insurance
      claim we will photograph the damage before anything is touched and describe it in
      writing for the loss adjuster, which is usually what decides whether a claim is paid.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-carbon">Where to find us</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-graphite/80">
      The office is at {company.office.line1}, {company.office.line2}, {company.office.town}
      {" "}{company.office.postcode}. It is for post and paperwork - surveys happen at your
      house, not ours. Open {company.hours}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Testimonials />
  <CallStrip />
</Layout>
